T6.text:
Add an `error_source` filter for debugging: it accepts the rendered string of a Jinja `TemplateSyntaxError` and returns the one template line shown as the source excerpt, with the error formatter’s leading display indentation removed; return an empty string if no source excerpt is shown. Example: `e = TemplateSyntaxError("bad", 2, "page.html"); e.source = "ok
{{ user.name }}
"; error_source(str(e))` should return `{{ user.name }}`. Another example: `e.source = "ok
    {{ item }}
"` should return `{{ item }}`.
